Good morning,

We are instructed to notify an ammonia release and consequent product loss on behalf of our client Harborline Cold Storage & Logistics, LLC. Our reference is TR/PROP/2025/4471.

Policy number: CP-4471-88210
Insured name: Harborline Cold Storage & Logistics, LLC
Date of loss: 10 January 2026
Loss location: 2870 Patapsco Industrial Parkway, Baltimore, MD 21226
Cause: Ammonia release - weld failure on a liquid ammonia header
Estimated loss: USD 3,700,000

A welded elbow on the liquid ammonia header failed overnight on Saturday. The
plant tripped as designed and Baltimore City Fire HAZMAT attended. Product in
three freezer rooms is presumed contaminated and a 31-hour temperature
excursion followed before rental cooling was cut in.

Most of the product at risk is customer-owned and stored under warehousing
agreements, so there is a bailee element as well as our client's own stock.
Nine of their customers have been notified. There is also water damage in the
engine room from a defrost line that split during isolation.

Emergency mitigation is running at about USD 140,000 to date and is ongoing.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * refrigeration engineer's report
  * product loss schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster today - our client has product
at risk and a customer notification obligation running. I am on +1 410 555 0182
if it is easier to talk it through.

